{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of volatility: The model assumes a smooth, near-linear trajectory, but true outcomes exhibit high-amplitude oscillations (spikes to ~100 and drops to ~87). Apply a volatility multiplier to forecast ranges rather than point estimates.",
    "Implement aggressive mean reversion after sentiment spikes: When sentiment history shows positive spikes (e.g., 0.33) followed by price surges, the model fails to anticipate the subsequent sharp correction. Reduce forecasts by 3-5% in the 5-10 day window following any price spike above 95.",
    "Adjust for momentum lag: The model consistently lags behind the initial breakout phase (e.g., the rise from 89 to 95). Add a momentum acceleration factor to the first 5 days of the forecast horizon when the 18-day history shows a steep upward trend.",
    "Incorporate sentiment decay: Positive sentiment values (0.20, 0.33) correlate with short-term price peaks that the model misses. If sentiment > 0.20, increase the immediate 1-day forecast by 2-3% but schedule a steeper decline in the 10-15 day horizon to match the observed mean reversion.",
    "Avoid over-smoothing long-term horizons: The model's 30-day forecast is too flat. Introduce a cyclical component to the forecast to capture the recurring ~10-day boom-bust pattern evident in the true outcomes."
  ]
}
